## Deliverables & Proposed Changes

### 1. Hazard Operational Contracts & Availability Matrix
Create standardized, strongly typed contracts for all 6 core hazard families defined in the blueprint:
- **Precipitation**: (Heavy rainfall, dry spells, flash flood potential proxy)
- **Tropical Cyclone**: (Bay of Bengal / Arabian Sea track, intensity, landfall)
- **Monsoon & LPS**: (Monsoon depressions, low-pressure systems, onset/withdrawal)
- **Western Disturbance**: (Northwest India mid-latitude troughs, winter precipitation)
- **Heatwave**: (Maximum temperature exceedance, persistent heat events)
- **Severe Wind**: (Gale force wind, 10m wind gusts)

#### [NEW] [data/hazard_availability_matrix.json](file:///c:/Users/adity/OneDrive/Desktop/SIH26079-RII/data/hazard_availability_matrix.json)
Machine-readable matrix specifying for each hazard:
- `hazard_id` and `hazard_family`
- `provider` (e.g. Open-Meteo GEFS 31-member ensemble, GFS, IMD/NCMRWF proxy)
- `variables` and canonical `units` (Kelvin, Pascal, m/s, mm/24h)
- `grid` resolution and domain
- `issue_time` and `valid_time` cadence
- `ensemble_size` (e.g. 31 members)
- `missingness_threshold` (maximum tolerable missing ensemble members)
- `latency_hours` (expected dissemination latency)
- `reference_source` (ERA5, IMD Gridded, IMD Best Track)
- `label_definition` and operational `thresholds`
- `operational_status`: `OPERATIONAL`, `PROXY`, `ABSTAINED`, or `FUTURE`

#### [NEW] [backend/app/contracts/hazard_contracts.py](file:///c:/Users/adity/OneDrive/Desktop/SIH26079-RII/backend/app/contracts/hazard_contracts.py)
Pydantic v2 schemas and validation models for:
- `HazardType`, `OperationalStatus`, `HazardContract`, `HazardAvailabilityMatrix`
- Contract lookup and validation functions ensuring upstream weather ingestion complies with hazard specifications.

