### 2. Target & Reference Manifests
Formalize canonical targets and ground truth sources to prevent data leakage and ensure reproducible evaluation.

#### [NEW] [data/target_manifest.json](file:///c:/Users/adity/OneDrive/Desktop/SIH26079-RII/data/target_manifest.json)
- Canonical definition of `bust_95th_mad` (stratified 95th percentile absolute error threshold).
- Hazard-specific target definitions:
  - `precipitation_exceedance_20mm`, `precipitation_exceedance_50mm`
  - `cyclone_track_error_100km`, `cyclone_intensity_error_15kt`
  - `heatwave_tmax_exceedance_40c`, `heatwave_tmax_anomaly_4_5c`
  - `severe_wind_gust_exceedance_17ms` (gale threshold)
- Invariant: Targets are strictly calculated against verified post-valid-time ground truth and never accessible at issue time.

#### [NEW] [data/reference_manifest.json](file:///c:/Users/adity/OneDrive/Desktop/SIH26079-RII/data/reference_manifest.json)
- Authoritative reference sources:
  - `ERA5_REANALYSIS` (ECMWF, 0.25° grid, 5-day latency, hourly)
  - `IMD_GRIDDED_RAINFALL` (0.25° × 0.25°, daily 03:00 UTC, India domain)
  - `IMD_GRIDDED_TEMP` (1.0° × 1.0° / 0.5° × 0.5°, daily maximum/minimum)
  - `IMD_BEST_TRACK` (Tropical cyclones in North Indian Ocean)
  - `STATION_OBS_GHCND` (Global Historical Climatology Network daily)
- Truth sealing contracts and access protocol rules.

